DESCRIPTION:\nIn our conversation partners program\, you can practice a la
 nguage one-on-one with a native speaker—and make a new friend! \n\n\nWe w
 ill match you with an IU Bloomington student or staff member who can help
  you learn a language that interests you\, and who wants to learn your la
 nguage. You and your partner will talk and write in both languages. Becau
 se your partner will be a native speaker\, you will learn how to use the 
 language in daily conversation. You will learn about each other’s culture
 \, too. The matching process is based on the number of applicants and ran
 ge of spoken languages.\n \nYou and your partner will meet at least once 
 a week during the semester. You can meet whenever and wherever you want. 
 Feel free to try out locations other than campus buildings\, such as coff
 ee shops\, American or international restaurants\, parks\, or the IU Art 
 Museum.\n \nThe application deadline his Sunday\, September 13\, 2026. Th
 is program is for current IU students\, staff\, and faculty. Apply HERE. 
 \nThis is a first come first serve program so apply early for the best ch
 ance to be matched with someone.\nYou will be notified if you have been m
 atched via email.\n\n\nHosted by: \n\nOnline Location: https://docs.googl
 e.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSeOUGDi07rJKXTvzq0vli7x61yj5xro96nfhQPRFE_e8Krm7A/
 viewform?usp=dialog\n\nAdditional Information can be found at: https://be
 involved.indiana.edu/event/12688420
DTEND:20260914T035900Z
DTSTAMP:20260905T041536Z
DTSTART:20260903T210000Z
LOCATION:Online
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Conversation Partners: Application Open
UID:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12688420
URL:https://beinvolved.indiana.edu/event/12688420
END:VEVENT
